    "note": "A bright piano register: six stiff partials rather than twenty rendered ones, with the inharmonicity that tells a piano from an organ.",
    "notes": {
      "inharmonicity": "A real string is stiff, so its nth partial is at n*f*sqrt(1 + B*n^2). B is about 0.0004 in the middle of a piano and rises towards the top.",
